  "agent_descriptions": [],
  "final": "`GET /files/<name>` now returns the signed-in user's own file as `text/plain; charset=utf-8`. All 6 tests pass, including 3 new ones.\n\n- **Auth:** the existing 401 check applies, so requests without a valid token are rejected.\n- **Scoping:** lookups only read from the caller's own directory. Bob requesting Alice's file gets a 404, not a 403, so the response doesn't reveal that the file exists.\n- **Invalid names:** names that fail the upload-time `valid_name` check (`..`, anything with a slash or backslash, anything starting with `.`) also get a 404. So do names containing a NUL byte and names that aren't regular files. The tests cover `/files/../bob/b.txt`, `/files/..`, an embedded NUL and the empty name.\n- **Headers:** I added `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`, so a browser won't render an uploaded file as HTML.\n\nThe change is a new `storage.read()` in `files_app/storage.py` and a route in `files_app/app.py`. I also added a line for the endpoint to `README.md`. I haven't committed anything.",
